<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Camadevivamsa</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">15th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Chamadevivamsa</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Camadevivamsa is a Pali chronicle written by the monk Bodhiramsi in Chiang Mai, probably in the early 15th century. It tells the legendary history of Queen <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chamadevi">Camadevi</a> and the founding of Haripunjaya, the Mon kingdom at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lamphun">Lamphun</a> that preceded Lan Na, and of the Buddhist relics enshrined there.</p></div>
